<title>BELGIUM: EU ministers allow Italy to repay farm co-op debt.</title>
<headline>EU ministers allow Italy to repay farm co-op debt.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Union farm ministers unanimously agreed to allow Italy to pay off the 100 million Ecus debts of 348 bankrupt farm cooperatives, EU officials said.</p>
<p>Unanimous agreement, reached in Luxembourg on Wednesday, was needed to override the European Commission's objections to the move.</p>
<p>The Commission argued that the Italian government's plan to pay off the debts over 10 years was against EU state aid rules.</p>
<p>--Brussels bureau +322 287 6830</p>
